# `ex_sd16b W, 0x58, 0x04` (and v7's `.byte 0xc1, 0x58, 0x04, 0x30`) is `ex (0x458:16), w`:
# llvm-mc assembles that spelling to c1 58 04 30 and unidasm reads the bytes as `ex (0x0458),W`.
s/^\tex_sd16b W, 0x58, 0x04$/\tex (0x458:16), w/
s/^\tex_sd16b\tW, 0x58, 0x04$/\tex\t(0x458:16), w/
s/^\t\.byte 0xc1, 0x58, 0x04, 0x30$/\tex\t(0x458:16), w/
